    "long_instructions": "**☑️ Do This:**\r\n\r\n- Under `# TODO: Defining Inputs`, define `inputs`, your feature matrix.\r\n- Under `# TODO: Defining Outputs`, define `outputs`, your labels.\r\n  - Be sure to cast numeric data using `int`, because it is given to you as a string.\r\n\r\n**💻 Coding Tip**\r\n\r\nRemember you can use `create_matrix` to combine your encodings into a feature matrix. It accepts a list of your encodings as input.\r\n\r\n```\r\nfeatures = [encoding0, encoding1, ...]\r\ninputs = create_matrix(features)\r\nprint_matrix(inputs)\r\n```\r\n\r\nRemember `outputs` should be a list of values representing what you’re trying to predict. You can use a simple list comprehension on `data` to create `outputs`.\r\n",
